          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What is described as first-line treatment for chronic insomnia?",
          "answer": "The first-line treatment for chronic insomnia is cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia (CBT-I). This approach is preferred over medication because its effects often persist after treatment ends, while the benefits of medication generally do not last as long. CBT-I consists of several components delivered as a package over four to eight sessions, including strategies like stimulus control and sleep restriction (reference: \"Chronic insomnia: cognitive behavioral therapy as first-line treatment\").\n\nIt's important to note that while CBT-I is the first-line treatment, sleep hygiene practices alone do not qualify as effective treatment for chronic insomnia (reference: \"Sleep habits for insomnia: what the daily routine actually looks like\"). \n\nIf you have more specific questions about the therapy or types of sleep issues, feel free to ask!\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
